  ba59ab5188 Restructure docs into per-kind spec and architecture homes (#9532)
  0ac0819414 Ignore gosu Go-stdlib false positives in docker scan (#8984)
  ba59ab51885 (Mihailo Markovic 2026-08-27 16:55:28 +0300  1) # grype configuration for the docker-image vulnerability gate (§AR-scan-docker-images).
  0ac0819414e (Mihailo Markovic 2026-07-07 12:20:31 +0200  2) #
  0ac0819414e (Mihailo Markovic 2026-07-07 12:20:31 +0200  3) # grype auto-loads this file from the repository root, so it applies to the
  0ac0819414e (Mihailo Markovic 2026-07-07 12:20:31 +0200  4) # `checkAllowedDockerImages` / `GrypeTask` scan both on PRs (changed images) and
  0ac0819414e (Mihailo Markovic 2026-07-07 12:20:31 +0200  5) # on the weekly all-images run.
  0ac0819414e (Mihailo Markovic 2026-07-07 12:20:31 +0200  6) #
  0ac0819414e (Mihailo Markovic 2026-07-07 12:20:31 +0200  7) # Every rule below suppresses ONE confirmed false-positive High/Critical finding
  0ac0819414e (Mihailo Markovic 2026-07-07 12:20:31 +0200  8) # in the Go stdlib statically linked into `/usr/sbin/gosu`. gosu is a ~200-line
  0ac0819414e (Mihailo Markovic 2026-07-07 12:20:31 +0200  9) # setuid shim that only calls setuid/setgid/execve to drop privileges and exec
  0ac0819414e (Mihailo Markovic 2026-07-07 12:20:31 +0200 10) # the container entrypoint; it does not invoke any of the affected stdlib
  0ac0819414e (Mihailo Markovic 2026-07-07 12:20:31 +0200 11) # subsystems (net/http, crypto/tls, crypto/x509, net/url, encoding/gob,
  0ac0819414e (Mihailo Markovic 2026-07-07 12:20:31 +0200 12) # archive/*), so none of these CVEs are reachable through it. gosu ships this
  0ac0819414e (Mihailo Markovic 2026-07-07 12:20:31 +0200 13) # stdlib upstream, so there is nothing for us to patch.
  0ac0819414e (Mihailo Markovic 2026-07-07 12:20:31 +0200 14) #
  0ac0819414e (Mihailo Markovic 2026-07-07 12:20:31 +0200 15) # Each rule is pinned to vulnerability id + package stdlib + version go1.22.2 +
  0ac0819414e (Mihailo Markovic 2026-07-07 12:20:31 +0200 16) # location /usr/sbin/gosu. Consequences of this narrow scope:
  0ac0819414e (Mihailo Markovic 2026-07-07 12:20:31 +0200 17) #   - a NEW go1.22.2 stdlib CVE (an id not listed here) is still reported;
  0ac0819414e (Mihailo Markovic 2026-07-07 12:20:31 +0200 18) #   - the same CVE in any OTHER binary/path is still reported;
  0ac0819414e (Mihailo Markovic 2026-07-07 12:20:31 +0200 19) #   - once gosu is rebuilt against a newer Go, the version pin no longer matches
  0ac0819414e (Mihailo Markovic 2026-07-07 12:20:31 +0200 20) #     and every finding re-surfaces for re-evaluation (acts as an implicit expiry).
[tool-exec] end id=call_mx8PLhNW350whtnGvTeugc5G|fc_06396d1a9acda5c0016a988c6dddc887d2ab62fdd189e05c08 name=bash status=success
